Tue Oct 27 21:14:11 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- Update to 2026.10.6:
  * An optional default that makes the Firefox theme the theme of
    every Firefox profile created from then on; existing profiles
    keep their theme
  * An optional default that gives Plasma Login Manager's login
    screen the Halloween background
  * Picking the global theme in System Settings now brings the
    colour scheme too
- Add the halloween-openSUSE-plasmalogin-defaults and
  halloween-openSUSE-firefox-defaults subpackages; the login
  background ships in halloween-openSUSE-plasma

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Tue Oct 20 12:43:00 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- Update to 2026.10.5:
  * New app icons by Pablo Herranz Ramírez: a code editor for
    vscodium, codium and vscode, chat bubbles for Slack, Polari
    and NeoChat, and the mail and music icons for Thunderbird
    and Spotify; kde/ now links 560 names to Breeze Dark
  * tools/check.py --release now also checks that every master
    in art/source/ is listed by a record in art/prompts/
  * The Firefox theme changes only in its version number
  * The new artwork is CC-BY-SA-4.0 like the rest; no licence,
    path or packaging changes
- adwaita-icon-theme description: it also serves Sway

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Tue Oct 20 06:10:51 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- Update to 2026.10.4:
  * Plasma keeps Breeze's own icons for names that only start like
    a file type's, such as the tray's volume icon, microphones,
    speakers, image-missing and the brightness applet; kde/ now
    links 548 names to Breeze Dark
- Changes in 2026.10.3:
  * A Sway edition: window colours, borders and gaps for Sway, a
    Waybar stylesheet and a SwayNotificationCenter theme
  * One-colour icons for the bell, notifications and
    SwayNotificationCenter's empty list
  * Plasma's battery applet keeps Breeze's icons for blocked and
    unblocked sleep
- Add the halloween-openSUSE-sway-theme subpackage; the GTK 3 theme
  and the Adwaita icon variant now also come with Sway

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Mon Oct 19 19:20:01 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- Update to 2026.10.2:
  * One-colour icons for more GNOME Settings rows: Users, Screen
    Lock, Location, File History & Trash, Diagnostics, Proxy,
    Pointing and Clicking and Screen Time
  * One-colour icons come hinted for 16 px
  * GTK 4 now draws the one-colour icons with its own faster parser
- Changes in 2026.10.1:
  * Icons for KDE System Settings' modules and categories,
    one-colour icons for GNOME Settings' panels, and one-colour
    twins of the settings icons Plasma uses in trays and menus
  * Plasma shows Breeze's own icons where it took the theme's for a
    longer Breeze name (battery, KWin effects, YaST modules): a new
    kde/ folder links most of them to Breeze Dark's, and the
    generic yast and blueman-device icons are dropped
  * Settings lists no longer show the same icon twice on one page
  * The GTK 3 theme is LGPL-2.1-only throughout
- The icon theme requires kf6-breeze-icons (also to build) for its
  kde/ links even without Plasma, so GNOME and Xfce get it too
- Run tools/check.py in full, with reuse's licence lint; follow
  upstream's floors: Pillow 11.3, jsonschema 4.24 and
  license-expression 30.0

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Mon Oct 19 16:19:33 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- Initial package 2026.10.0: an autumn Halloween theme for
  Plasma 6, GNOME 50 and Xfce 4.20: wallpapers, two icon themes,
  Plasma, SDDM, Plymouth, GTK 3/GNOME Shell/Xfce and Firefox
  themes, and SDDM and GNOME defaults; the halloween-openSUSE
  metapackage pulls in the pieces for the installed desktops
- Build the Firefox theme as its own flavor that requires the
  same-architecture MozillaFirefox, since Firefox loads it only
  from its architecture-specific directory; the rest is noarch

